        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 68-year-old male patient, admitted on 19 December 2020 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray confirming hyperinflation without pneumonia, arterial blood gas analysis revealing hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia, and pulse oximetry monitoring throughout the stay. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. Treatment consisted of supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. The patient responded well to therapy with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 20 December 2020 in stable condition with oral prednisolone taper, inhaled bronchodilators, and written action plan. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
